| group | sample_row | value | rank |
| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| x | 0 | 1 | 1.0 |
| x | 1 | 2 | 2.5 |
| x | 2 | 2 | 2.5 |
| y | 0 | 3 | 4.0 |
| y | 1 | 4 | 5.0 |
| y | 2 | 5 | 6.0 |


| label | statistic | p_value |
| :--- | ---: | ---: |
| normal approximation | 0 | 0.076523 |

\image(figures/hypothesis_ranks.svg)
// result_end

\caption(Average ranks expose the tie correction. The two equal x observations coincide in the plot but remain separate rows in the table.)
\alttext(Values one, two, three, four and five map to pooled ranks one, two and a half, four, five and six; x and y have distinct colours.)

>> Three groups and an ANOVA decomposition

Take \((1,2,3)\), \((4,5,6)\) and \((7,8,9)\). Group means are two, five and
eight; each within-group sum of squares is two. Hence \(SS_W=6\),
\(SS_B=3(2-5)^2+3(8-5)^2=54\), and \(F=(54/2)/(6/6)=27\).
The uncorrected pooled rank sums are six, fifteen and twenty-four, giving \(H=7.2\).
There are no ties, so its tie factor is one. The two procedures answer different mean
and rank-distribution questions and use different reference assumptions.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/hypothesis_anova.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
const std::vector<double> values={1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9};const std::vector<std::size_t> sizes={3,3,3};
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame d;d.add_column("group",std::vector<std::string>{"A","A","A","B","B","B","C","C","C"});d.add_column("value",values);
  const auto summary=d|dm::group_by("group")|dm::summarise(dm::agg::n("n"),dm::agg::mean("value","mean"),dm::agg::sd("value","sample_sd"));
  auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();plot.points({1,1,1,2,2,2,3,3,3},values,"observations",{37,99,235});
  plot.segments({.8,1.8,2.8},{2,5,8},{1.2,2.2,3.2},{2,5,8},{220,38,38},3);
  plot.title("Three means, equal within-group spread").x_label("group index: A, B, C").y_label("measurement").x_limits(.5,3.5).y_limits(0,12);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");plot.size(820,470).save_svg("build/hypothesis_anova.svg");
  std::print("{}\n\n{}\n",summary|dm::to_md(),dm::stats::hypothesis_test_table({dm::stats::one_way_anova(values,sizes),dm::stats::kruskal_wallis_test(values,sizes)},{"classical ANOVA","Kruskal-Wallis"}).select({"label","statistic","parameter1","parameter2","p_value"}).to_md(6));
}
```
