\caption(Three groups have equal sample SD one and means two, five and eight. ANOVA F equals 27; Kruskal-Wallis H equals 7.2.)
\alttext(Three vertical strips contain values one to three, four to six and seven to nine. Short red lines mark each group mean; tables give group summaries and both test results.)

>> Ten coin trials: exact tails and a non-dual interval

For \(n=10,p_0=1/2\), observing nine successes selects counts \(0,1,9,10\)
in the two-sided probability ordering. The p-value is
\((1+10+10+1)/2^{10}=22/1024\). At 5%, the same four counts are the full rejection
region, so the null rejection rate is 0.021484375, below the nominal 0.05.

For the separate asymmetric null \(p_0=0.3\), observing zero successes gives a
probability-ordered p-value about 0.03884, while the equal-tailed 95% Clopper–Pearson
interval extends to about 0.30850. It contains 0.3 even though this two-sided test rejects.
Neither calculation is contradictory: the interval and test use different orderings.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/hypothesis_binomial.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
const auto region=dm::stats::binomial_rejection_table(10);auto mass=dm::graphics::RPlot::create(),pvalues=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  mass.bars(region.numeric_column("successes").values(),region.numeric_column("null_probability").values(),"null PMF",{37,99,235});
  const auto selected=region.filter([](const auto& r){return r.get_double("reject_exact")==1;});
  mass.bars(selected.numeric_column("successes").values(),selected.numeric_column("null_probability").values(),"5% rejection region",{220,38,38});
  mass.title("Binomial(10, 0.5) null outcomes").x_label("successes").y_label("probability").y_limits(0,.38);
  pvalues.lines(region.numeric_column("successes").values(),region.numeric_column("exact_p").values(),"exact",{37,99,235});
  pvalues.lines(region.numeric_column("successes").values(),region.numeric_column("score_p").values(),"corrected score",{220,38,38});
  pvalues.abline_h(.05).title("Two-sided p-values").x_label("successes").y_label("p-value").y_limits(0,1.35);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(mass).add(pvalues).size(1100,490).fit_panels().save_svg("build/hypothesis_binomial.svg");
  std::print("{}\n\n{}\n",region.to_md(6),dm::stats::hypothesis_test_table({dm::stats::binomial_test(9,10),dm::stats::binomial_test(0,10,.3)},{"9/10 vs 0.5","0/10 vs 0.3"}).select({"label","p_value","ci_lower","ci_upper"}).to_md(6));
}
