>> A 2x2 table small enough to enumerate

For the observed table \((0,3;3,0)\), every margin is three. The top-left count can be
zero, one, two or three, with probabilities \((1,9,9,1)/20\). Both endpoint tables
are as improbable as the observed one, so Fisher's two-sided p-value is 0.1.
Pearson expected counts are all 1.5, giving uncorrected \(X^2=6\) and Yates-corrected
\(X^2=8/3\). Their asymptotic p-values differ substantially; these small expected
counts do not justify choosing the uncorrected approximation because it rejects.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/hypothesis_fisher.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
const auto support=dm::stats::fisher_exact_support(0,3,3,0);const auto tail=support.filter([](const auto& r){return r.get_double("selected")==1;});
  auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();plot.bars(support.numeric_column("top_left").values(),support.numeric_column("probability").values(),"conditional null",{37,99,235});
  plot.bars(tail.numeric_column("top_left").values(),tail.numeric_column("probability").values(),"selected tail",{220,38,38});
  plot.title("Four tables with the same margins").x_label("top-left count").y_label("conditional probability").y_limits(0,.65);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");plot.size(820,470).save_svg("build/hypothesis_fisher.svg");
  std::print("{}\n\n{}\n",support.to_md(6),dm::stats::hypothesis_test_table({dm::stats::fisher_exact_test_2x2(0,3,3,0),dm::stats::chi_squared_test_independence({0,3,3,0},2,2,false),dm::stats::chi_squared_test_independence({0,3,3,0},2,2,true)},{"Fisher conditional","Pearson asymptotic","Yates asymptotic"}).select({"label","statistic","p_value"}).to_md(6));
}
```
