Four-comparison family:

| label | mean_difference_cm | ci_lower | ci_upper | p_value | holm_p |
| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| Sepal.Length | -0.652 | -0.881973 | -0.422027 | 1.866144e-07 | 3.732289e-07 |
| Sepal.Width | -0.204 | -0.330284 | -0.077716 | 1.819483e-03 | 1.819483e-03 |
| Petal.Length | -1.292 | -1.495490 | -1.088510 | 4.900288e-22 | 1.470086e-21 |
| Petal.Width | -0.700 | -0.795100 | -0.604900 | 2.111534e-25 | 8.446138e-25 |

\image(figures/hypothesis_iris_location.svg)
// result_end

\caption(Petal-length distributions and four raw-unit mean-difference intervals. Holm-adjusted p-values belong to the declared four-Welch-test family; the displayed 95% intervals remain marginal.)
\alttext(Three species boxplots show different petal-length levels and spreads. A second panel shows versicolor-minus-virginica differences and marginal confidence intervals for each of four measurements.)

The versicolor-minus-virginica petal-length difference is -1.292 cm, with marginal
95% interval [-1.49549, -1.08851] cm and Holm-adjusted p-value about 1.47e-21.
All four mean differences remain distinguishable from zero within this declared family;
the largest adjusted p-value is 0.00182 for sepal width. These effect estimates describe
the sampled groups under the stated model.

>> Pooled association is not within-species association

Sepal and petal length are paired measurements on each flower. The pooled Pearson and
Spearman results combine between-species and within-species variation. We show each
species' separate coefficient alongside the pooled results, and colour the scatter by
species to make that mixture visible. These additional exploratory p-values are not
members of the preceding four-test family and are not called multiplicity-adjusted.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/hypothesis_iris_association.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
const auto d=dm::datasets::iris();std::vector<dm::stats::HypothesisTestResult> pearson,spearman;std::vector<std::string> labels={"pooled"};
  const auto x=d.numeric_column("Sepal.Length").values(),y=d.numeric_column("Petal.Length").values();pearson.push_back(dm::stats::pearson_correlation_test(x,y));spearman.push_back(dm::stats::spearman_correlation_test(x,y));
  auto scatter=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();const std::vector<std::string> species={"setosa","versicolor","virginica"};const std::vector<dm::RGB> colors={{37,99,235},{220,38,38},{22,163,74}};
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<species.size();++i){const auto g=d.filter([&](const auto& r){return r.get_string("Species")==species[i];});const auto gx=g.numeric_column("Sepal.Length").values(),gy=g.numeric_column("Petal.Length").values();labels.push_back(species[i]);pearson.push_back(dm::stats::pearson_correlation_test(gx,gy));spearman.push_back(dm::stats::spearman_correlation_test(gx,gy));scatter.points(gx,gy,species[i],colors[i]);}
  scatter.title("Pooled and within-species association").x_label("sepal length (cm)").y_label("petal length (cm)").y_limits(0,9);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");scatter.size(820,490).save_svg("build/hypothesis_iris_association.svg");
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame::MarkdownOptions fmt;fmt.digits=6;fmt.scientific={"p_value"};
  std::print("Pearson:\n\n{}\n\nSpearman (t approximation):\n\n{}\n",dm::stats::hypothesis_test_table(pearson,labels).select({"label","estimate1","ci_lower","ci_upper","p_value"}).to_md(fmt),dm::stats::hypothesis_test_table(spearman,labels).select({"label","estimate1","p_value"}).to_md(fmt));
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Pearson:

